<h1 class="tcs-policy-title">Refund and Returns Policy</h1>
<div class="entry-content">

<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Every sleeve we sell is printed to order with your design, after you approve a free digital proof. Because of that, we do not take back sleeves for a change of mind. We do put things right when an order arrives defective, damaged or misprinted. This policy explains how.</p>
<hr />
<h3>Who This Policy Covers</h3>
<p>This policy applies to every order we ship. We ship to addresses in the <strong>United States only</strong>.</p>
<hr />
<h3>What We Replace or Refund</h3>
<p>We replace or refund sleeves that are:</p>
<ul>
<li><p><strong>Defective</strong>: a printing or manufacturing fault, such as smudged ink, bad cuts or a seam that does not hold</p></li>
<li><p><strong>Damaged in transit</strong>: sleeves that arrive crushed, wet or torn</p></li>
<li><p><strong>Misprinted</strong>: sleeves that do not match the proof you approved, such as wrong artwork, text or size</p></li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h3>How to Report a Problem</h3>
<ul>
<li><p>Email <a href="mailto:info@thecoffeesleeves.com">info@thecoffeesleeves.com</a> within <strong>14 days of delivery</strong>.</p></li>
<li><p>Include your order number and <strong>photos</strong> of the problem and of the shipping box.</p></li>
</ul>
<p>In most cases the photos are enough and you do not need to send anything back. If we do need the sleeves returned, we email you a prepaid return label, so <strong>we pay the shipping</strong>. There is no restocking fee.</p>
<hr />
<h3>Replacement or Refund</h3>
<p>Once we approve your request, you choose:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>A <strong>free replacement</strong> of the affected sleeves, printed and shipped to you at no cost, or</p></li>
<li><p>A <strong>refund</strong> for the affected sleeves, issued within <strong>10 business days of approval</strong> to your original payment method (PayPal or bank transfer), in US dollars.</p></li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h3>What We Cannot Accept</h3>
<ul>
<li><p>Returns for a change of mind on sleeves that were printed correctly to your approved proof</p></li>
<li><p>Errors that were in the artwork you approved, such as a spelling mistake on the proof</p></li>
<li><p>Sleeves damaged after delivery, or used sleeves</p></li>
<li><p>Problems reported more than 14 days after delivery</p></li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h3>Cancellations</h3>
<p>You can cancel free of charge at any time before you approve your proof. Once the proof is approved and the order goes into production, it cannot be cancelled.</p>
